PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Strong consensus (8/14 colleagues) on B as the minimal change: add TSO post-UMI on beads to enable 5'-RACE/template-switch capture of TCR V(D)J-CDR3 during RT/PCR. This directly fixes the 3'-poly(dT) bias problem where CDR3 lies hundreds of nt upstream of constant-region 3' end (beyond reliable 225 bp Read 2 coverage). Preserves BD Rhapsody beads, cell-label/UMI architecture, AbSeq/Sample-Tag compatibility, and fixed 75x225 sequencing. BD commercial TCR workflow uses essentially identical TSO strategy. 

Minority views: C (3) or A (2) advocate TCR-specific capture oligos on beads (flanking CDR3 or upstream of VDJ) but still anchored to 3' workflow; D (1) relies on post-capture PCR primers that cannot recover sequence never captured. All keep 3'-bias so cannot guarantee CDR3 inclusion. E ruled out by cost constraint.

Unresolved: exact oligo placement/PCR nesting details for B; whether existing Rhapsody AbSeq panels tolerate TSO addition without re-optimization. No factual errors noted; B aligns with TCR transcript architecture and constraints.}

