PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Strong round-1 consensus (9/14) still favors B (TSO after UMI) as the only constraint-compliant fix for 3'-poly(dT) bias: CDR3 hundreds of nt upstream of constant 3' end lies outside 225 bp Read 2; TSO enables 5'-RACE/template-switch during RT/PCR, placing CDR3 in the window while preserving BD Rhapsody beads, cell-label/UMI, AbSeq/Sample-Tag/mRNA panels, and fixed 75x225. Matches commercial BD TCR workflow exactly. 

Opposition (Colleagues 1,5,7,9,13,14) pushes C (or A) arguing TSO introduces RT/PCR chemistry changes risking cross-talk, yield loss, or barcode issues in multiplex panels; C's flanking TCR oligos on beads avoid new enzymes and keep poly(dT) intact. Pro-B replies: A/C still 3'-anchored so cannot guarantee upstream sequence; bead redesign incompatible with existing validated workflow.

Unresolved: exact TSO placement/nesting PCR details; empirical tolerance of multi-panel Rhapsody runs to TSO addition (no data yet). No factual errors; B remains technically decisive under stated constraints.}

